{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0d2754ddca67e98ab8cda0456f6e501d6e1d106083c97a0ab10ec10b4670a440","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d31ab055a21de4b43b5574cab516455efb05ea00e04ab550b58ac71a442004c8"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"In routed mode, loopernet centralizes webhook ingress and Node wakeups but must not mutate GitHub on its own; the Coordinator writes coarse GitHub authority first and the exact target label last, with polling retained as fallback and drift recovery.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1687f9c1480f50ea69278c56d1a9b58ef63133317f19e4d809b7e42904df59d1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f97da3f5eaf6312f9ab13153e70eb4cfed892dcd924fd85e495bca36bfebc838"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"The webhook forwarder lock uses OS file locking and is not designed for NFS-style shared filesystems; the documentation advises keeping the runtime directory on a local filesystem.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_17067f6373093d983efed565d17754e67050c5091ab0cc4b6e16fca260ca3019","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_25807d0122c7d564dc4925f3db1e9ffa3766de6d112ffa6d6ae6137c9164ba88","slc_68731cd7717d8c231946eff51d0ea012c06ffa2907578e0afb1b353e3def3b31","slc_6d5464705351e2343ae6545377242d9f1f1a1c74eb11beb1a9ae131aabd4df05","slc_9d124614eb96df768dd5f7a66f6a7070572c9dcca8cfa81d0233cc5668d73005","slc_a068611223328909f08392c96715c3f4a2957f13040d733c64096dea3cbc471c","slc_d646a862a40fe786e304d408356802804da8510108b64977ac63cc68617256dd"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Looper is distributed as a GitHub Release Go binary and supports multiple agent vendor CLIs identified in config, including grok-build (invoked as grok), pi, and omp (Oh My Pi), alongside codex and claude-code shown in examples.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1e441d515b435f94340b7859f8a56ff8fbcb537bfc7ac9c8434bec7c56c4449c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1bc4250db3538c33a6d7f4eaff0bc344f754a65e29b0f7498369951b38a60320"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"For fresh unattended Grok Build runs, Looper supplies --always-approve and --sandbox off by default; configured agent arguments override these, so operators may choose a stricter --sandbox, and non-plain output formats can break result-marker parsing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_208db7d532595cb122787bfd6b96a785211c6eb94c9170911b515036b4889b2f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9d124614eb96df768dd5f7a66f6a7070572c9dcca8cfa81d0233cc5668d73005","slc_a36b11acb048bdb791fb0d19f48fa0cfb020bf03362caac7db07a358b98d1ee4"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"looper daemon install places a managed daemon binary at ~/.looper/bin/looperd; daemon start writes a pid file and lifecycle diagnostics under ~/.looper, and the CLI looks up the daemon there before $PATH.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_292680c748d1670ac28aedd0052e62a9252e6e7b529916779274ea66cf7725fc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_02096f2e83eb95f13d721fe180f581074dc3704b5f380a7aedf93f7267e9cb84","slc_1cc8d2a7b2faecf83d06d2944a3e276bfa68aeb99bb0147f958fac2481e22cb6","slc_d58aab7ab542ad17405b5b4a0811409abc798179c94133df12690ca224a2cac1"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Agents read repository data through a host CLI exposed as LOOPER_HOST_CLI with subcommands such as host whoami, host api, host threads, and host git; these commands require the execution's private socket and cannot select another account or repository.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2aefc41857077948a65f55d692d4ebb99d8100cdcff298bf5ab8303319b50160","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_68d176b9ce5cb517c3228519e3103bcf02824f675150356287686d773bc466c6","slc_6ca503de948ed08e00386fe5d94d0d3a88f86ceaf74b26fb3f7aec52d8e4d491","slc_d1cb63615640e6465ea867485319256aacc3d59f91e429b8ae5fe729308ced3b"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Webhook support has two delivery modes: gh-forward (default), where Looper runs gh webhook forward per repo and receives deliveries on the daemon route /webhook/forward, and tunnel, where Looper creates per-repo GitHub webhooks and the user supplies a tunnel to 127.0.0.1:<listenPort>.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2b03def758431262b11849f0b9fd44e81d202d45fd90289d0a7f511fdeac6c2a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6b4f49f5d3ec03b0e76a646976fe7966cc5fb33fcb592e3cd42ad393a01f0f6c","slc_b8c8428bd958d5a078b29f7057e313a7d7e910e41e0b6528e1438a55bd1b711e","slc_fa3ce74daac5e7ef65af04ad4196ecfc0e0a8adae0abd6cda225d08df75b77a4"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Grok Build, Pi, and Oh My Pi support is fresh-run only: daemon native resume and interactive takeover via looper resume are unsupported, and retries use a fresh checkpoint prompt.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_327ad4891c627340c019af77f775f723eacfd176f6940e049e4f7fd82c39998f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7a55857017067a570e337d29116ad9b8a6cee8ddb28a8cd17b21306e6569b678","slc_aceba412f71a3eac37500f9ba5eb5683b34d37bddd144fac45bc5c257b18b8f9","slc_c37ed17bddd73ac854af6f5270bdfb12aeffaca957513cf7773d3aeff63f0f98"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"In-flight runs keep the immutable config snapshot and durable per-run agent snapshot they started with; resume/retry lineages copy the predecessor's agent_snapshot_json rather than re-resolving live config, and Looper never sends an old vendor's native session ID to a different CLI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_33510f04398d5d87c84278c34c84610ac97b305ae4ddb872591ac0bde9100669","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_73dad6b1d8d22b5fbc4b991c79d2060206aef3bcce28a876ffba2a0eedb3f3de","slc_b97873c636b0cf4f3c73dfba36269362bd396ae1db9e156bdbfbea8fe751671b","slc_f362eda07587576aa1e1efde0e721e31e78e220a16d0c70c2241df0327c2cdd1"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Per coding role, agent identity overlays global agent.vendor/model, then the role's selected profile, then role-inline vendor/model, with inline winning per field; a role is runnable only when the overlay leaves a non-empty vendor.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_36f1b8280eb229a3852db6aae30e72fd77f6a1a97830b20f0fde2ad64bab7037","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36260a8ce3b32fc1463dea8d7a2f6805992f70572ffd994d59590d56bd88b397","slc_50f171928fa6a4391c79c52a6f9b47e9f204f5a7ac1329718af0a4a11ac6dd05"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Repository development practice: a separate sandbox-e2e CI workflow runs on main and manual dispatch using a repository variable and secret for a GitHub App, mints an installation token via actions/create-github-app-token, and cleans up temporary issues, PRs, and branches afterward.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4a1e274932f1f34c6611ee3c7b3981617ec65ffb3b8b077282c7b4eda835c8a3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0879c9477c3b579f70efc7e291958248acfd341ed8c4c16678423b2a8175bdd5","slc_1fed9211bca96495f21023513048cd21625cf8302e0c66b19a5968c7d9e9de08","slc_f75746b1b5be40405fda9b54ff54eacc05ea11524e1b1cb83dce28114056a774"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"looperd loads configuration in layers: built-in defaults, config file, environment variables, then CLI flags; later layers override earlier ones, objects merge deeply, arrays are replaced as a whole, and omitted fields keep the previous layer's value.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6b6c4a321b979c0cb0da0fbb70e84b2e5af98bb216ff8996428d1242fdd49fe9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3ba9441939f920a1429f52ad0893aca817b4f519248652828192a00d0c6dae20","slc_443c88d75e30ba4f2373ab90089df66ba2bef6d5be45079246a859c5f10cd1d9"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"[[projects]] entries are a declarative startup import: the daemon validates and transactionally imports them into SQLite and builds the runtime Project Catalog exclusively from active database records; config import never removes API-managed projects, and reusing an API-managed ID fails startup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_743410e6ed68dd8f74cc248988a8f74bb66e6881ceb1d81a53341d4c7d6a78b1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9fee22dcd3cae0aa71a1b6c540efc9f6234d7b0ec8a5b8a109d4c7c20023fe22","slc_d58aab7ab542ad17405b5b4a0811409abc798179c94133df12690ca224a2cac1"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Hosting tokens, private-key references, and personal GitHub/SSH authentication are stripped from agent environments after overrides merge; credential-bearing Git/GitHub CLI commands have a four-minute ceiling, and this is a credential/command-routing boundary rather than an OS sandbox.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9eca3f56534053d98aeb81b6b10d9e4c6da2ded81c0f5d87ea8ccad425b9cdb8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_66a04a18a6759636108f4afd3d5c6a5305f7c214cd9d2e7ad8ebdf4b3d38f748","slc_6cbea7c45589a1981aaa8d212129b5636fb2e2dc4fad48da74902f07831ba5b7","slc_a60a6c3025f0beb9fcdc2b346f9f3df2c1613760a20b44c6b70a13dffcb18c9f"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Projects have two network modes: off (local-only, looper:target:* labels ignored) and routed, where multi-Node operation is coordinated through loopernet and exactly one looper:target:<node_name> label is the exact-Node authority.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a98d9ad9568075703fc5df839fbbc186c6033cf0ea83a896f5251f97ffadb501","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0c84c2256162eae452534c3782c2151127daaf07820c8334cad831467397ad8d","slc_71629a9aacb03106a32d5be1c167b3f3a19115e893835cd448e57d42ed8a4ca8"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"looperd watches the config file and atomically publishes a candidate only when every changed effective field is hot-safe per an explicit allowlist; invalid or restart-bound-containing candidates are rejected as a whole, leaving the last-known-good snapshot active with diagnostics at /dashboard/config.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bf75fce2a2d98a741554c33acc4f95d5b3a9fec770b625e46b46505bceb24acf","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f90f2d53c76fe89d97577bdc979560a574a827e2828e1129e10868a5cce12d0","slc_6f928ec989249a0fa97203d2f24807403e878e492b2972bcc2465bbdb43a60b6"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"The daemon exposes a dashboard config editor at /dashboard/config and a PATCH /api/v1/config endpoint; every patch must submit the revision of the file generation that produced the published values, and when token auth is unset the endpoint accepts only loopback peer/Host requests and rejects proxy-forwarding headers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e449e277691a622dc235dda0ce8d9a23c16ebb6e121905066a90dc264947b632","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"nexu-io/looper@141510c0967f snapshot 3ca8b4de5320199a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6dd5c7895b4cf5f2d101e7fc9309faa3de74de4638d0aa594249b76eae00fae1","slc_9211e23ee33fe5e28f4eb5be7ba91e0e56b7eff01e1a2e17dbbea086b647b816"],"source_ids":["src_f4c2257a910c5ff99710c169e15bbb10"],"text":"Model suggestions are served via GET /api/v1/agent/models?vendor=..., combining a built-in per-vendor static list with an optional best-effort probe of the local vendor CLI; the catalog is advisory only, not an allowlist, and arbitrary model IDs remain valid.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:21:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cb3f52ff97144c59b2b248e1866d1c2f"}
